(CareBridge Project Report - Sample PDF) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Chapter 1: Introduction) Tj T*
(CareBridge is a healthcare management system written in modern C++.) Tj T*
(Patients can register, find nearby hospitals, browse doctors and) Tj T*
(book appointments. Doctors can triage appointment requests and) Tj T*
(maintain electronic health records for their patients.) Tj T*
(The system serves two hospitals in the demo data set: CityCare) Tj T*
(General Hospital and Riverbend Medical Center.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
3 0 obj
<< /Length 566 >>
stream
BT /F1 13 Tf 56 760 Td 18 TL
(Chapter 2: Data Structures Used) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A singly linked list stores patients, doctors and appointments,) Tj T*
(giving constant-time insertion but linear-time search.) Tj T*
(A priority queue orders appointment requests so that Emergency) Tj T*
(cases are seen first, then Urgent, then Routine requests.) Tj T*
(A queue delivers patient notifications in first-in first-out order,) Tj T*
(while a stack tracks each doctor's recently viewed patients.) Tj T*
(Merge sort ranks hospitals by distance in O\(n log n\) time.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
4 0 obj
<< /Length 509 >>
stream
BT /F1 13 Tf 56 760 Td 18 TL
(Chapter 3: Results and Future Work) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The prototype handles one thousand synthetic patients with ease.) Tj T*
(Booking a slot and confirming it takes under fifty milliseconds.) Tj T*
(Future work includes a real database such as SQLite or Postgres,) Tj T*
(proper password hashing with bcrypt, and a mobile application.) Tj T*
(Telemedicine video calls are planned for the second release,) Tj T*
(scheduled for March 2027 according to the project roadmap.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
